Id: stor010w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Blacklist firewire-core, firewire-ohci and ohci1394 in /etc/modprobe.d.
References: modprobe.d(5)
Controls: NIST MP-7; ISO 7.10

FireWire can be used, and the policy is to have none. A device on a
FireWire bus reads and writes memory directly, no operating system
in the way: whoever plugs one in owns the machine. Blacklist the
stack (firewire-core, firewire-ohci and the legacy ohci1394) where
nothing on the bus is needed.
